title: "Estimated Daily Visitors to Siesta Key Beach"
format: html
execute:
  echo: false
  message: false
  warning: false
---

## A rough daily average

A local vacation-rental provider reports an estimate of **2.2 million visitors
per year** to Siesta Key Beach. Dividing by 365 days gives an annualized
average of about **6,027 visits per day**.

```{r}
library(tidyverse)

daily_estimate <- tibble(
  estimate = "Annualized daily average",
  annual_visitors = 2200000
) |>
  mutate(visitors_per_day = annual_visitors / 365)

ggplot(daily_estimate, aes(x = estimate, y = visitors_per_day)) +
  geom_col(fill = "#2D7FA3", width = 0.55) +
  geom_text(
    aes(label = scales::comma(round(visitors_per_day))),
    vjust = -0.5,
    size = 5
  ) +
  scale_y_continuous(
    labels = scales::label_comma(),
    limits = c(0, 7000),
    expand = expansion(mult = c(0, 0.02))
  ) +
  labs(
    title = "About 6,000 beach visits per day",
    subtitle = "Annual estimate of 2.2 million visits divided by 365 days",
    x = NULL,
    y = "Estimated visits per day",
    caption = "Source: Gulf Coast Vacation Rentals; this is an annualized estimate, not a daily head count."
  ) +
  theme_minimal()
```

This is a rough average, not a claim that the beach gets the same number of
visitors every day. The published annual estimate does not describe its
counting method, and actual attendance likely changes by season, weather, and
day of the week.

## Source

- [Gulf Coast Vacation Rentals: Siesta Key beach facts](https://www.gcvacationrentals.com/florida%C2%92s-top-rated-beach-siesta-key/) —
  reports 2.2 million annual visitors.

